{
  "requirement": "`habeas add-input --file-range <file>:<start>-<end>` MUST add or refresh one file-range input containing the current raw lines in the inclusive range. It MUST reject a missing file or invalid range.",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "**Implementation is largely sound.** The {impl} markers are present on `add_input`, `selectors_for_mode`, `update_inputs` and `InputSelector::resolve`.\n- `selectors_for_mode` in `src/add_input.rs` parses `<file>:<start>-<end>`. It rejects a missing colon or dash and non-numeric bounds.\n- `InputSelector::resolve` in `src/inputs.rs` reads the file with `read_project_file`. That call fails for a missing or disallowed file. `resolve` also rejects a range when start is 0, end is before start, or end is past the file's last line.\n- It stores the raw lines `lines[start-1..end]`.\n- `update_inputs` finds an existing input with the same selector and then reports it as unchanged or refreshed, or appends it as added.\n\n**Tests do not cover the rejection obligations.** The two tests marked {test} for this requirement are in `tests/commands.rs`:\n- `add_input_external_sources_respect_allow_and_disallow` uses `--file-range <abs>:1-1`. It checks the success path with an allowed external file, and it checks that a disallowed path is rejected. It also asserts the stored `file`, `line_start`, `line_end` and `text`.\n- `add_input_modes_capture_raw_sources_and_refresh_idempotently` runs `--file-range src/main.rs:1-2` and only asserts success. Its later assertions check input counts and the text of the rust-item input (`inputs[1]`). It never asserts the file-range input's content. It also never re-runs a file-range add to check the refresh or unchanged behaviour.\n\nI found no test of `add-input --file-range` with any of these cases:\n- a nonexistent file;\n- a malformed spec;\n- start 0;\n- end before start;\n- end past EOF;\n- non-numeric bounds.\n\nThe only rejection test of this kind, `file_ranges_report_order_eof_length_and_missing_file_errors` in `tests/evidence_boundaries.rs`, covers CI validation of recorded evidence. It does not cover the `add-input` command. The \"MUST reject a missing file or invalid range\" half of the requirement therefore has no test. Refreshing a changed file range is also untested. These gaps are not marked with any FIXME.",
